course: dictionary
lesson: 15808
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. The words around a word give you clues about which meaning the writer means. Read the sentence first, then ask: which meaning fits here?
explain: «Mia left the glue uncapped, and by Monday it had dried hard.» The clue is glue left open. Here uncapped means without a lid or cap on top.
explain: «The council set uncapped fees for parking, so the price could rise with no limit.» Here uncapped means with no upper limit. News about money uses the word this way.
explain: «Our club signed an uncapped player who had never played for his country.» In sports news, a cap is one match for your country. So uncapped means a player who has not yet played for their national team. This is the third meaning.
fact: Uncapped has three main meanings: without a lid, without an upper limit, and, in sport, never yet picked for your country.
fact: «Uncapped» means without a cap or lid on top, as in «an uncapped bottle».
fact: «Uncapped» means with no upper limit, as in «uncapped fees».
fact: In sport, a «cap» is one match played for your country, so an uncapped player has not yet played for the national team.
fact: To check a meaning, put it into the sentence in place of the word. If it still makes sense, you have probably found the right one.
exercise: «The pen was left uncapped all night.» What does uncapped mean here? | Never picked for a team | Without any upper limit | Very cold | *Without a lid on top
exercise: «The company offered uncapped bonuses to its best workers.» What does uncapped mean here? | Never played for a country | Without a lid | *With no upper limit | Shiny and new
exercise: Ella reads that a footballer is uncapped. What does this tell her? | He is the best player in the league | He has a hat on his head | *He has never yet played for his national team | He has just been sent off
test: «Ruby was thrilled to be picked for her first match, even though she was still uncapped.» What does uncapped mean here? | *Never yet played for her country | Very tired | Without a lid | No limit on her age
test: «The fees are uncapped, so the price could rise by any amount.» What does uncapped suggest? | Covered with a lid | Free of charge | Sold out | *No upper limit on the price
exam: «The coach named three uncapped players in the squad.» What does uncapped mean here? | With no upper limit | *Never yet played for their country | Very old | Without a lid
